{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119053","id":3597677951,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7WcDV_","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119053","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119053.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119053.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119053","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119053/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119053/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119053/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/936d67b7c7573044061c493a72ea956c0d6e33e3","number":119053,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix area light texture color conversion","user":{"login":"LiveTrower","id":48926464,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4OTI2NDY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/48926464?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower","html_url":"https://github.com/LiveTrower","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiveTrower/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR fixes the color conversion specifically for mip 0 of the area light textures.\r\n\r\nFrom what I understand, the texture passed to the `area_texture` property is in sRGB. When it is copied to the atlas, the conversion to linear space is not performed, which causes the texture to look washed out when rendered.\r\n\r\n|Washed out ❌|Correct ✅|\r\n|--------|--------|\r\n|<img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"before\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/17e9474f-3388-4353-95b0-27ad5e4ea60f\" />|<img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"after\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aefe47cc-88c2-4db6-81b4-d192268e052d\" />|\r\n\r\n|Atlas Mip 0 (sRGB)|Atlas Mip 0 (Linear)|\r\n|--------|--------|\r\n|<img width=\"256\" height=\"256\" alt=\"atlas_before\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/295f5985-f356-43e8-be7a-4c04cdd98e82\" />|<img width=\"256\" height=\"256\" alt=\"atlas_after\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f7bf504b-3b97-45b9-9fbb-76161c39a947\" />|\r\n\r\nThis does not happen with the mipmaps because the conversion to linear is handled during the Gaussian filter application. This results in an inconsistency when transitioning from mip 0 to mip 1.\r\n\r\n|Mip transition|Atlas Mip 1 (Linear)|\r\n|--------|--------|\r\n|<img width=\"256\" height=\"150\" alt=\"before2\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d84e344b-70ae-4920-90e0-d60896047b2d\" />|<img width=\"128\" height=\"128\" alt=\"mip\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1730a2db-eb5a-4350-959b-9a1e61f2fbb8\" />|\r\n\r\nThe solution I implemented was using `rd_texture_srgb` instead of `rd_texture`. While it might not be the ideal approach, it is simple and practical.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengin